// The 20-case drafter eval — citation coverage and false-claim rate (spec §8.15, WP-15c).
//
// Read-only. Nothing in eval/drafter-cases.ts writes to this file.
//
// `provenance` is on every row and is load-bearing: "scripted" means this text was written by hand against
// the prompt contract, because docs/HUMAN_TODO.md H-02 is open and there is no live output to commit. A
// row marked "live" came from a real run. See eval/drafter-cases.ts for why the test prints which it scored.
//
// Eight cases a well-behaved model would write, twelve designed to trip one specific rule each. The
// twelve are the point: a drafter eval with no defects in it measures nothing.




{"id":"clean-01-unauthorised","text":"A fully cited note for a valid passkey chain.","reason":"UNAUTHORISED","amountMinor":12999,"currency":"USD","chainValid":true,"webauthn":true,"provenance":"scripted","modelText":"The deterministic Dispute Defender decided this case under rule R-UNAUTH-1 [[clm_rule]]. The buyer is disputing USD 129.99 [[clm_dispute_amount]]. Our records show that the chain verified [[clm_chain_verified]]. The signed purchase record is in the attached packet. https://countersign.example/v/pkt_01HQ0000000000000000000000"}
{"id":"clean-02-inr","text":"Fully cited, INR, so the currency rule has to read a real rupee amount.","reason":"UNAUTHORISED","amountMinor":129900,"currency":"INR","chainValid":true,"webauthn":true,"provenance":"scripted","modelText":"The buyer is disputing INR 1299.00 [[clm_dispute_amount]]. The signed order totals INR 1299.00 [[clm_order_amount]]. The signed purchase record is in the attached packet. https://countersign.example/v/pkt_01HQ0000000000000000000000"}
{"id":"clean-03-jpy","text":"Fully cited, JPY, which has no minor digits at all.","reason":"UNAUTHORISED","amountMinor":5000,"currency":"JPY","chainValid":true,"webauthn":true,"provenance":"scripted","modelText":"PayPal captured JPY 5000 [[clm_capture_amount]] in capture 3ABCLEAN-03 [[clm_capture_id]]. The signed purchase record is in the attached packet. https://countersign.example/v/pkt_01HQ0000000000000000000000"}
{"id":"clean-04-refunded","text":"Fully cited with a completed refund, so the refund claims exist and are used.","reason":"UNAUTHORISED","amountMinor":12999,"currency":"USD","refunds":[{"amountMinor":12999,"status":"COMPLETED"}],"chainValid":true,"webauthn":true,"provenance":"scripted","modelText":"We refunded USD 129.99 [[clm_refund_amount_0]] on PayPal refund REF-0 [[clm_refund_id_0]]. The signed purchase record is in the attached packet. https://countersign.example/v/pkt_01HQ0000000000000000000000"}
{"id":"clean-05-registered-tracker","text":"Fully cited, and the tracking claim is a PayPal-held record.","reason":"UNAUTHORISED","amountMinor":12999,"currency":"USD","tracking":{"carrier":"DHL","number":"JD0002000031","registered":true},"chainValid":true,"webauthn":true,"provenance":"scripted","modelText":"Our records hold tracking DHL JD0002000031 [[clm_tracking_shp_1]]. The signed purchase record is in the attached packet. https://countersign.example/v/pkt_01HQ0000000000000000000000"}
{"id":"clean-06-quotes-own-status","text":"Quotes the SHIPPED status we actually hold, which is reporting rather than asserting delivery.","reason":"UNAUTHORISED","amountMinor":12999,"currency":"USD","tracking":{"carrier":"UPS","number":"UP9911","registered":true},"chainValid":true,"webauthn":true,"provenance":"scripted","modelText":"Our records show the shipment status SHIPPED [[clm_tracking_status_shp_1]]. The signed purchase record is in the attached packet. https://countersign.example/v/pkt_01HQ0000000000000000000000","_note":"The mirror of bad-08-forged-status: the same claim id, the value we hold rather than the value a model would prefer to write."}
{"id":"clean-07-two-claims-one-sentence","text":"Two claims in one sentence, which is the shape a real model produces and a per-sentence checker has to handle.","reason":"UNAUTHORISED","amountMinor":12999,"currency":"USD","chainValid":true,"webauthn":true,"provenance":"scripted","modelText":"The deterministic Dispute Defender decided this case under rule R-UNAUTH-1 [[clm_rule]]. PayPal captured USD 129.99 [[clm_capture_amount]] in capture 3ABCLEAN-07 [[clm_capture_id]]. The signed purchase record is in the attached packet. https://countersign.example/v/pkt_01HQ0000000000000000000000","_note":"Replaced a no-passkey case: R-UNAUTH-3 decides REVIEW, so the router refuses to file it and the drafter is never reached. That is the router running first, and it belongs in the router eval rather than this one."}
